A||||22||EdsB52||Royalty for a day||||1||
Z||000000||EdsB52||09-30-2001||04:39 AM||||I went to the Diamondback game on Friday where Gonzolas hit a solo HR in the bottom of the 11th. It was awesome, and the fact that I had about $350 parlayed into the game didn't hurt anything either! When I was acquiring the tickets, I found that seats worth having were going to cost at least 100 bucks, so I went for the best since they cost $150 each. It was Matt Williams bobblehead night, so that was more motivation. Anyway, I bought 2 tickets for my girlfriend and me and we headed out. As I bought the tickets, the scalper told me Jerry Colangelo sits right behind where we will be sitting. I naturally thought he was full of it. When we got there, he was right, along with Colangelo's bodyguard and all his yes-men. It was wild, we had our own section with our own bathrooms and bar (not that I drink) and restaurant. It was amazing the number of rich folks that go to the game so they can hang around the bar inside the tunnel and not watch the game. Most of the people in the section I was in were there for status; I was there because they were some of the best seats in the house. Most of the older women were the Linda Evans type and the young girls were the supermodel type. All of the other people were very civilized and proper, whereas I was a typical routy blue-collar guy. I don't know that they appreciated my candor about the opposing team or the ref's poor calls! It was unique rubbing elbows with the elite for a night though.||||reg||1
Z||000001||hugh||09-30-2001||07:50 AM||||Glad you enjoyed yourself.Did any of those poor unfortunates own a Fiero?As far as the elite,I always picture them sitting on the toilet,and all of a sudden they're the same as me.||||reg||1
Z||000002||maryjane||09-30-2001||12:40 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by hugh:<BR><B>Glad you enjoyed yourself.Did any of those poor unfortunates own a Fiero?As far as the elite,I always picture them sitting on the toilet,and all of a sudden they're the same as me.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><BR>Hugh,you must have a lot of control over your imagination. Something just won't let me visualize another guy sitting on a toilet.<BR>ED, they may not have appreciated your candor, but I bet they heard it!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"> Always wanted to splurge on something like that, just never could justify spending the $$$$. <BR>||||reg||1
Z||000003||hugh||09-30-2001||04:44 PM||||I picture them like that,but not in detail(thank GOD).It just lets me know that no one is always dignified.||||reg||1
Z||000004||frontal lobe||10-02-2001||01:38 PM||||Going to a baseball game sure has changed, hasn't it?  When player salaries were lower, income generated by baseball FANS was enough to pay them.  Now that salaries are so exhorbitant, teams need to find more income than what just fans of the game can or will generate.  So they try to make just GOING to the park an event, whether you are a fan of the game or not.  <P>I bet it was quite interesting being with the "beautiful people".  It's kind of fun and interesting in its way for a short period of time, but if you are around it too long and you start to see how misguided their priorities are, you start to pity them in a way.  For example, they probably didn't even care about the Matt William's bobbing head doll!!  And on the way to their cars, ask them who won the game.  Think they would know?<P>Glad you had fun.||||reg||1
Z||000005||EdsB52||10-02-2001||05:52 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by frontal lobe:<BR><B>Going to a baseball game sure has changed, hasn't it?  When player salaries were lower, income generated by baseball FANS was enough to pay them.  Now that salaries are so exhorbitant, teams need to find more income than what just fans of the game can or will generate.  So they try to make just GOING to the park an event, whether you are a fan of the game or not.  <P>I bet it was quite interesting being with the "beautiful people".  It's kind of fun and interesting in its way for a short period of time, but if you are around it too long and you start to see how misguided their priorities are, you start to pity them in a way.  For example, they probably didn't even care about the Matt William's bobbing head doll!!  And on the way to their cars, ask them who won the game.  Think they would know?<P>Glad you had fun.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>"For example, they probably didn't even care about the Matt William's bobbing head doll!!  And on the way to their cars, ask them who won the game.  Think they would know?"<P>Good points. Like I wrote, half the 'special' patrons were inside the lower bar oblivious to what the game was doing. As far as the parking, we had our own lot that was a stones throw from the park. It had about6 levels and my girlfriend counted 3 'ugly' cars in that whole structure. They were a bunch of pretentious *******, but I could sure get used to their lifestyle. Most of the true fans were up in the $6 seats. ||||reg||1
Z||000006||Raydar||10-02-2001||06:07 PM||||This reminds me of a concert I went to a couple of years ago.<BR>Several years ago, Grand Funk Railroad did a benefit concert for Bosnia, in Detroit. It went over so well that they decided to go back on tour. They played at a concert venue in Atlanta called Chastain Park Amphitheater(sp?). <BR>Having grown up listening to GFR, I *had* to go see them.<BR>Place was armpit deep in "Wine-and-Cheeseheads". Not that I have anything against wine and cheese, but this was a freakin' rock and roll concert. Not a night at the opera. All these folks wanted to do was socialize.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/mad.gif"> Yeesh!<P>------------------<BR>Raydar - aka Steve<BR><FONT SIZE="1"><BR>Black 88 Formula.<BR>Red 88 Duke coupe. "The Project" <BR>88 Formula parts car. "The Donor"<BR></FONT>||||reg||1
Z||000007||RiceCooker||10-02-2001||07:41 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by hugh:<BR><B>As far as the elite,I always picture them sitting on the toilet,and all of a sudden they're the same as me.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>That's perfect hugh  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>I liked this post, i'm not sure why but it does say a heck of a lot.||||reg||1
