Z||000015||frontal lobe||10-03-2001||10:50 PM||||Sorry, Hugh.  The changers and wipers INSIST on NO creamed corn.  Apparently makes clean up TOO difficult.<P>Hey EdsB52, little-remembered Matt Williams fact:  when he was with the Giants, he was on pace to break Babe Ruth's home run record when baseball went on strike that year ('94?), thus ruining his chance.  I remember he had over 40 at the time they called the season off.  Of course, he would have held it only a few years, we know now.<P>Is Barry Bonds going to make it?||||reg||1
Z||000016||maryjane||10-04-2001||12:33 AM||||Boy, this thread has literally turned to sh**.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"> Eds comment seemed pretty innnocuous to me. I think he just meant that they think their u-know-what don't stink. Brought to mind the bathroom valets they had in all the bars in Korea and the Phillipines tho. What a crappy way to make a living  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><BR>Barry Bonds? Yes, I think he will and a few more to boot. Surprised it took him this long.||||reg||12
Z||000017||EdsB52||10-04-2001||11:56 AM||||   <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by JSocha:<BR>[B][/B]<HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>"Oh!  Thank you for that clarification Ed, if not to me then to the general populace here.      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/rolleyes.gif"><P>Certainly not to you, as I owe you nothing, but I wanted to ensure Hugh I meant absolutely nothing against him. In fact, I think his analogy was quite funny and insightful; kind of like they say to do when you're publicly speaking and nervous about it; envision everyone naked. These 'beautiful people' still go to the dentist (except Mick Jagger and Benny Hill), have pap smears or colon examinations, and take a crap. They can't contract that duty off to another lowly working-class sap, although I'm sure they wish they could. I merely expounded on good insight.<P>"However, I still personally feel the original comment you made above still reflects a sense of      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_bs.gif">    , no matter what rationale now has been placed behind it by you to justify stating it as it is, in the form it had been presented in the first place.      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif">"<P>I won’t place any rationale behind anything, but I will say you’re on an island. If you still have residual dismay over the post where I refute Christianity’s role in America as not being as positive as advertised, then go find that post and constructively answer those points, unless you can’t, then you need to take your residual anger to another post and misdirect it here.<P>“Funny thing is, I recall somebody else recently in another thread apologizing to you after you commented to his post, as you apparently must have read into it far more then I (or perhaps anyone else for that matter) did, for something, which in my opinion, was less to not offensive at all in the first place.<P>Hint:  Arizona Dreamy Draw Dam Thread...when somebody asked for your "help/assistance" since you were in the area as well.<P>Now compare the specific comment of that thread asking for assistance to the way you have your comment above shown here and ask yourself, who is going to find the "comedic proposition" that you wanted to relay with the way it is specifically presented above.”<P>If you had any integrity, you would post whatever statements to which you are referring and contextualize them. I don’t want to reopen a can of worms, as you are, but in order to defend myself I must identify the statements. A member wrote:<P>"Like I said I could use a little help from some people around here It would be nice to have EDSB52 jump in and offer to help me get the info that is needed with out stiring things up." <BR>And then I responded with:<BR>“You want some kind of positive response with a plea like that? Nice job stirring things up yourself.” <BR>The thread was: <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum6/HTML/003128.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum6/HTML/003128.html</A> <P>Now please, I hope no one looks up that post as I have spoken on the phone with the gentleman that wrote that harmless statement about possibly going to the dam and I think he’s a good guy. I needed to post that statement because JSocha opened it up as if there were harsh words between a member and me. <P>Now back to JSocha. You claim to be your company’s sh!thouse lawyer and you’re too lazy to archive an old post? It took me 5 minutes at the most. Do you realize what being a lawyer is all about? You might research an issue for hours or days before you’re satisfied you can make 1 assertion. Then as you have a collection of these assertions, you can make an argument. I don’t know what flew up your panties JSocha, but I wish you would remove it. OK, I compare the statements, which are far different from each other, and I find no similarities. <P>“Ed, just so you understand, I am not trying to get into a "p*ssing" match with you or against you, as it is definately unnecessary, even if it appears to you that way or that I am, because I am not.”<P>Does anyone else see what I see by JSocha’s statement? It looks like a double-negative disclaimer written by a neurotic schizophrenic. Pick a side of the fence JSocha. You’re obviously the only one that sees my remark as defamatory to Hugh, so why don’t you just let it go? <P>“I am only commenting on the way the comment itself is presented and it just does not stand well or reflect the "comic" intention that you may feel you had.  <P>It looks to me as a personal attack on Hugh who originally made a comment.”<P>I know it looks that way to you JSocha, now go back to the Christianity post and write a response.<P>“And by the way Hugh responded, it's apparent he did not see the humor in it as well and may have taken it as an attack against him.<P>Just my 2 cents Ed, take it and or leave it.”<P>I don’t think so. Oh, and I’ll leave it.<P>PS.  Thanks for opening an old can of worms, I only hope it doesn't lead to other dissention.<P>[This message has been edited by EdsB52 (edited 10-04-2001).]<p>[This message has been edited by EdsB52 (edited 10-04-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000018||EdsB52||10-04-2001||12:14 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by frontal lobe:<BR><B>Sorry, Hugh.  The changers and wipers INSIST on NO creamed corn.  Apparently makes clean up TOO difficult.<P>Hey EdsB52, little-remembered Matt Williams fact:  when he was with the Giants, he was on pace to break Babe Ruth's home run record when baseball went on strike that year ('94?), thus ruining his chance.  I remember he had over 40 at the time they called the season off.  Of course, he would have held it only a few years, we know now.<P>Is Barry Bonds going to make it?</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I didn't know that, but I'm fairly new to the baseball spectating world. Is he one of your favorite players? He had a good game that night, other than trying to run for a triple and getting thrown out at third. He's to old to be running for 3! <P>Bonds, no it doesn't look like it. In fact, Houston is so determined not to give up #70 that they hit him with a pitch, walked him twice, and gave him one ball to hit which I believe he grounded out a couple nights ago. It's kind of a rip and I think one could cite racial implications here. When McGuire was going for the record and Sosa was on his ass, a couple rookie pitchers threw him ducks which left the field. They pitched Sosa hard till the end. Now with Bonds, Houston has lost the last 2 games and might jeopardize their playoff standings trying to avoid giving him #70. The Giants play Houston tonight, then go to LA for 3, who is out of the playoff race and has said they won't stop play to celebrate #70 or #71 if hit. That tells me they won't throw him one hitable pitch. Bonds is the least popular player in baseball today and I don't know why. The fool that paid 3 million for McGuire's #70 is breathing a sigh of relief right now, albiet possibly temporary!||||reg||1
Z||000019||EdsB52||10-04-2001||12:20 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by maryjane:<BR><B>Boy, this thread has literally turned to sh**.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"> Eds comment seemed pretty innnocuous to me. I think he just meant that they think their u-know-what don't stink. Brought to mind the bathroom valets they had in all the bars in Korea and the Phillipines tho. What a crappy way to make a living   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><BR>Barry Bonds? Yes, I think he will and a few more to boot. Surprised it took him this long.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Thanks Don. With the brash retorts I've unfortunately rendered in the past, I'm surprised someone would think they need read into my posts, a hidden message. I'll generally come right out and say something nasty if I feel warranted. And I'm very glad that Hugh didn't take it wrong, thanks Hugh.<P>What would the Korean and Phillipino bathroom valets do? Or what would they not do?!||||reg||1
Z||000020||frontal lobe||10-04-2001||02:33 PM||||Even though I grew up in the Midwest (by geography, should have been a Cubs fan--ooh, baby!) I started rooting for the Giants when they had Willie Mays, Willie McCovey, Juan Marichal and even Barry Bond's father, Bobby.<P>So I've continued to follow them even though I enjoy baseball less due to the obscene salaries, general lack of effort, and I'm still bitter over the strike.<P>Matt Williams was on the Giants so I rooted for him.  I still root for him even though he is on Arizona, for the reason he signed a free agent contract with the D'Backs:  when he was looking at teams, he was just going through a divorce and his wife decided to move to Arizona, so he signed with them so he could be near his children.<P>And Matt, going for 3!!!  Come on, act your age!  You're an old dad now!||||reg||1
Z||000021||Cheever3000||10-05-2001||10:43 AM||||Don't nobody throw anything at me for bringing this back up, but...<P>... who's Jerry Colangelo?<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000022||EdsB52||10-05-2001||11:00 AM||||He's the guy that ruined the Phoenix Suns. He owned controlling interest in the Suns and did a Jerry Jones and let his ego run off guys like Barkley. Then his yes-***** , Cotton Fitzsimons, brings Barkley into the America West Dome and says, "see these seats? They were full before you got here, and they'll be full when you leave." Well, immediate and current history has proven to be that that isn't true. Then the team fell off and can't get out of the first round. After ruining the Suns, he then sold much of his interest in the team. Colangello also owns controlling interest in the Diamondbacks. He's quite a big figure in this town, that's why I liked acting like a frikin lunatic at the game, 15 feet away from him! I didn't offend anyone there and pulled for the home team, but my behavior was more blue-collar than caviar and tea.||||reg||1
